#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""sparktop — a live, top-style GPU monitor for the NVIDIA DGX Spark.

Pure stdlib. Reads telemetry from `nvidia-smi` (NVML), which is the only
interface that exposes GPU utilization/power/clocks on the GB10 superchip.

Usage:
    sparktop                 # live view, refresh every 1s
    sparktop -n 2            # refresh every 2 seconds
    sparktop --once          # print one snapshot and exit (good for scripts)
    sparktop --no-color      # disable ANSI color
    sparktop --ports 3000-3009,8080   # which ports to watch
    sparktop --no-services   # hide the systemd services pane
    sparktop --no-ports      # hide the listening-ports pane
    sparktop --no-air        # hide the air-quality pane
    sparktop --no-llms       # hide the local-LLMs pane
    sparktop --db PATH       # where the sqlite database lives
    sparktop --no-db         # don't record anything

Model servers running on the box (llama.cpp, ollama, vLLM, ...) show up in
an "LLMs" pane, with what each is serving and whether it's busy right now.

If an air-quality Feather is plugged into USB, its readings show up in an
"Air" pane. The board is found automatically via /dev/serial/by-id; point
sparktop at a specific port with --air-device or $SPARKTOP_AIR_DEVICE.

Every reading the board sends is also recorded in a local sqlite database,
$SPARKTOP_DB or ~/.local/share/sparktop/sparktop.db by default.

Override the nvidia-smi binary (handy for testing) with:
    SPARKTOP_NVIDIA_SMI=/path/to/fake-nvidia-smi sparktop
"""
